{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "האם", :translit "ha'im", :gloss "whether / if"} {:he "האם תמנו לגוע", :translit "ha'im tamnu lagua", :gloss "Have we come to an end, to perish"} {:he "האם אין עזרתי בי וגו'", :translit "ha'im ezerati bi vagomer", :gloss "Is my help not within me etc."} {:he "אעשה לו עזר כנגדו", :translit "e'eseh lo ezer kenegdo", :gloss "I will make for him a helper opposite him"} {:he "ותושיה נדחה ממני", :translit "vetushiyah nidchah mimeni", :gloss "and counsel is driven from me"} {:he "האם תמנו לגוע", :translit "ha'im tamnu lagua", :gloss "Have we come to an end, to perish"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["האם תמנו לגוע" "האם אין עזרתי בי"]}], :frame {:text "The verse Genesis 2:18 records 'I will make for him a helper opposite him' (אעשה לו עזר כנגדו), establishing marriage as a fundamental human need. The Talmud (Yevamot 63b) states that a man without a wife is called 'without good' and 'without help,' and (Yevamot 62b) that one who does not engage in procreation is considered as though he has shed blood and diminished the divine image. The Talmud (Berakhot 17a) similarly describes Torah study as essential for life, and the verse in Job 6:13 ('Is my help not within me, and counsel driven from me' — ותושיה נדחה ממני) links the loss of counsel (תושיה, associated with Torah wisdom per Talmud Shabbat 31a) to a state of loss. Job 10:21 describes the land of darkness as a place from which one does not return, connecting death with finality. The Ba'al HaTurim connects these traditions to Numbers 17:28 ('Have we come to an end, to perish' — האם תמנו לגוע), interpreting 'perish' as equivalent to spiritual death.", :sources ["Genesis 2:18" "Yevamot 63b" "Yevamot 62b" "Berakhot 17a" "Shabbat 31a" "Job 6:13" "Job 10:21" "Numbers 17:28"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["האם תמנו לגוע" "האם אין עזרתי בי"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "האם תמנו לגוע", :refs ["Numbers 17:28"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "האם אין עזרתי בי", :refs ["Job 6:13"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:29:58.721951791Z", :model "glm-5.2"}